    {
      "heading": "Fidelity Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "Fidelity offers self-directed brokerage accounts with no minimum deposit to open an account. Online trading commissions for US stocks, ETFs, and options are $0. Fidelity applies option contract fees on top of its $0 base commission, while buy-to-close option orders with a premium of $0.65 or less carry a $0 contract fee. For fixed-income securities, Fidelity lists secondary-market bonds at $1.00 per bond online. Fidelity also lists non-Fidelity no-transaction-fee (NTF) mutual funds at $0 online.\n\nFidelity fits investors who want $0 account minimums, zero-commission stock trading, and clear secondary bond pricing at $1.00 per bond. \n\nVersus Vanguard, Fidelity does not publish a per-contract dollar figure for options in its primary commission table, stating that contract fees apply. Vanguard publishes a $1-per-contract fee on accounts with QA under $1 million, while exempting options exercises and assignments from commissions. Vanguard assesses a $25 annual fee on accounts with QA under $1 million unless the account owner selects electronic document delivery or qualifies for an operational waiver.\n\nWorked cost example: Buying 10 secondary-market bonds online costs $10 at Fidelity ($1.00 multiplied by 10). On options, closing a contract priced at $0.50 costs $0 at Fidelity under its buy-to-close rule, whereas Vanguard lists a $1 contract fee on standard options trades for accounts with QA under $1 million."
