      "heading": "Webull Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "Webull provides self-directed trading accounts with $0 commissions for US-listed stocks, ETFs, and standard equity options. Webull requires no minimum initial deposit to open an account. Certain index options cost $0.50 per contract. Trading carries regulatory pass-through fees, including a Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) fee of $0.0000206 multiplied by trade volume. Webull charges $75 per outgoing stock transfer.\n\nWebull fits active retail investors and options traders who want $0 contract commissions on standard equity options with no deposit minimums.\n\nVersus Vanguard, Webull charges $0 in broker contract fees for standard equity options, compared to Vanguard's $1 per contract on accounts with QA under $1 million. However, Webull charges $75 for an outgoing stock transfer if an investor moves assets to another institution. \n\nWorked cost example: A trader executing 100 standard equity options contracts pays $0 in broker commissions at Webull, plus applicable regulatory fees. At Vanguard, 100 contracts cost $100 ($1 multiplied by 100) for accounts with QA under $1 million. If that trader transfers the entire stock account out of Webull, Webull assesses a $75 outgoing transfer fee. Vanguard applies a $25 annual service fee if the investor opts out of electronic delivery."
